========================================================================================
the quantifier trap: A* is PERIODIC in u for fixed (q,v)
========================================================================================
  A*_u is the least residue of 3^{-(u+1)} c mod 2^{n+1}, and
  ord_{2^{n+1}}(3) = 2^{n-1} for n >= 2, so u -> A*_u has period 2^{n-1}
  and dips to O(1) within every period.  Hence NO lower bound on A* holds
  uniformly in u for fixed (q,v).  This is harmless for Theorem U: for
  fixed n, bound (i) alone gives log2(r+1) >= u+1 = S-n+1, so the ratio
  tends to 1.  But a hypothesis must be stated for A*/2^{n+1} or
  equivalently relative to S -- never as an absolute floor on A*.
     (q,v)   n  period  periodic  min A* over a period
    (3, 1)   4       8      True                     5
    (2, 3)   5      16      True                     5
    (3, 4)   7      64      True                     5
    (2, 6)   8     128      True                     5

